.TH DIAG_FC 8 "June 2026" Linux "PowerLinux Diagnostics"
.SH NAME
diag_fc \- Fibre Channel diagnostics tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diag_fc
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.RI [ host ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diag_fc
is a diagnostic tool for monitoring Fibre Channel Host Bus Adapters (HBAs)
on PowerVM LPAR systems. It collects health metrics, detects issues, and
logs events to servicelog for proactive system maintenance.

The tool monitors:
.IP \(bu 2
Link state (Online/Offline/Linkdown)
.IP \(bu 2
Error counters (CRC errors, link failures, loss of sync/signal)
.IP \(bu 2
Performance metrics (frame/word counts, throughput)
.IP \(bu 2
Topology changes (LIP events, fabric changes)
.IP \(bu 2
EEH events (PowerPC-specific hardware errors)

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help message and exit.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I host
One or more FC host names to check (e.g., host0, host1).
If no hosts are specified, all FC hosts in the system will be checked.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Check all FC hosts:
.B diag_fc

.TP
Check specific hosts:
.B diag_fc host0 host1

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ppc64-diag/diag_fc.config
Configuration file for thresholds and monitoring options (installed from scripts/diag_fc.config).
.TP
.I /sys/class/fc_host/
Sysfs directory containing FC host information.
.TP
.I /var/log/ppc64-diag/
Log directory for diagnostic output.
.TP
.I /etc/cron.daily/run_diag_fc
Cron script for periodic execution of diagnostics.

.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The tool reports the following information for each FC host:
.IP \(bu 2
WWPN (World Wide Port Name)
.IP \(bu 2
Port state
.IP \(bu 2
Link speed
.IP \(bu 2
Error counters
.IP \(bu 2
Health status

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success - all checks passed
.TP
.B >0
One or more checks failed

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diag_nvme (8),
.BR diag_encl (8),
.BR servicelog (8)

